   "text": "# J Street pilot pitch\n\nDraft for the owners of [[J Street Gym]]. Numbers in brackets get filled from the pilot. Prices from [[Pricing]]; any change goes in [[Decisions]] first.\n\n## The pitch (one page)\n**The problem.** People follow a member in without scanning. Every one is a lost membership, and staff can't watch the door all night.\n\n**What SecurityAI does.** A small box by the camera recorder counts people at the door during the night hours and checks each entry against the front-desk check-ins. No video stored, no facial recognition, member numbers scrambled. See [[How SecurityAI works]].\n\n**The pilot.** First month free. Every flagged entry is checked by a person, so the count is confirmed tailgates, not guesses.\n\n**What we found.** [X] confirmed sneak-ins in [Y] nights, about [Z] a month.\n\n**The safety side.** Someone who follows a member in signed no waiver. If they get hurt, the insurer asks how they got in. SecurityAI gives the gym a record that it checks the door.\n\n**The math.** A sneak-in is worth about $10 here. SecurityAI is $200 a month per entrance, month to month. Catching 20 a month covers it; at [Z] a month that's about $[Z \u00d7 10] of lost membership found.\n\n**The ask.** Keep it running at $200 a month, cancel any time.\n\n## Before it's ready\n- [ ] Hardware in and first nights run. See [[Hardware readiness list]].\n- [ ] Real counts from the pilot month.\n- [ ] Turn the results into the [[J Street pilot case study]].\n- [ ] TJ reads it and makes it his own words.\n"
